    "['mpls te tunnel-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng 100', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng 100\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if referring to the tunnel interface configuration context in Cisco, it would be:\\n##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: Cisco's syntax depends on the context. The first version is commonly used when enabling MPLS TE features globally or in interface configuration mode. The second is more explicit and may be seen in some documentation. Both are functionally equivalent for this translation.\", 'trans_template': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng 100\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if referring to the tunnel interface configuration context in Cisco, it would be:\\n##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: Cisco's syntax depends on the context. The first version is commonly used when enabling MPLS TE features globally or in interface configuration mode. The second is more explicit and may be seen in some documentation. Both are functionally equivalent for this translation.\", 'trans_template': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100'}]]": 1,
